# TIDEPUP: the tide starter, and the mesh BRINEFIN and PUDDLIN tint.
# Y is up, +Z is the front, one world unit is one map tile. The lowest vertex
# sits on y = 0 and the model is centred on x = 0 and z = 0, so the game places
# it by its feet.
#
# Faces are wound so that (c - a) x (b - a) points out of the solid, which is
# what tools/obj2cpp.py bakes as the face normal. Get it backwards and the
# model still draws, it just goes flat ambient dark.
#
# Eyes are not modelled. They are two depth tested dots in the 2D layer, a
# pixel each instead of eight triangles.
#
# About 0.90 units tall, 84 triangles.
# A long low body, a big upswept tail fluke, and flippers where the
# front legs would be. Nothing else in the roster has a fluke, and the
# profile is the flattest of the six, so it never reads as a quadruped.

mtllib tidepup.mtl

# body, 24 triangles
v 0.000 0.630 -0.060
v 0.242 0.505 -0.060
v 0.121 0.505 0.315
v -0.121 0.505 0.315
v -0.242 0.505 -0.060
v -0.121 0.505 -0.435
v 0.121 0.505 -0.435
